A||||1||falconhulk||Squealing or hissing||||1||
Z||000000||falconhulk||11-13-2001||07:49 AM||||My car (85 se v6)has started this strange squealing but its high pitch and is the only sound you can really hear from the engine at idle after a long drive.  I mean its not super loud, but if you walk by the car thats all you hear.  It does not seem to be coming from a belt.  As a matter of fact its very hard to track the exact spot it is coming from!  Any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||JohnF||11-13-2001||08:03 AM||||Use a listening device such as piece of hose or a wooden stick.  Place one end of the device on any spot on the engine and the other end to your ear.  Listen for any abnormal sounds.  <P>I would start with the alternator (bad diodes can make a very high pitched squeal) and then go to any rotating component.<P>You'll very likely hear the offending part(s).||||reg||12
